Fix a data race that aborts airsim_node on its first publish.

The node creates a Reentrant callback group and spins it on a MultiThreadedExecutor, so
drone_state_timer_cb re-enters concurrently and several threads race on the shared
per-vehicle curr_odom_. Copying a std::string while another thread reassigns it is a torn
read, and Fast-CDR reports the result as:

    eprosima::fastcdr::exception::BadParamException: The string contains null characters

Evidence (drone-sim, 2026-08-01): a gdb backtrace put the abort in publish_odom_tf ->
TransformBroadcaster::sendTransform. Hex-dumping both frame ids there produced 862 prints
containing ZERO 00 bytes while it still aborted -- so no string ever held a NUL. 30% of
consecutive log timestamps were out of order, confirming concurrent execution of the
callback for a single vehicle.

MutuallyExclusive serialises the callback and fixes it. Verified: node survives, publishes
14 topics, odom_local flows.

This is an upstream defect and is worth reporting to Cosys-Lab.

NOTE ON LINE ENDINGS: Cosys-AirSim sources are CRLF. This hunk was GENERATED from the real
file rather than hand-written, because a hand-written LF hunk fails with
"Hunk #1 FAILED (different line endings)". Regenerate it the same way if it ever drifts.

--- a/ros2/src/airsim_ros_pkgs/src/airsim_node.cpp
+++ b/ros2/src/airsim_ros_pkgs/src/airsim_node.cpp
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
     nh->get_parameter("host_port", host_port);
     nh->get_parameter("enable_api_control", enable_api_control);
     nh->get_parameter("enable_object_transforms_list", enable_object_transforms_list);
-    auto callbackGroup = nh->create_callback_group(rclcpp::CallbackGroupType::Reentrant);
+    auto callbackGroup = nh->create_callback_group(rclcpp::CallbackGroupType::MutuallyExclusive);
     AirsimROSWrapper airsim_ros_wrapper(nh, nh_img, nh_lidar, nh_gpulidar, nh_echo, host_ip, callbackGroup, enable_api_control, enable_object_transforms_list, host_port);
 
     rclcpp::executors::MultiThreadedExecutor executor;
